Internship Task 2 Report
Project Name: Brag Board
Project Title: Building a Secure Login System and Department-Wise Dashboard using React, Tailwind CSS, and FastAPI
Submitted by: Battula Sruthi Keerthi
Under the Guidance of: Respected Madhuri Mam
Date: 9-10-2025
________________________________________
Task Objectives
1.	Build a clean and responsive layout using Tailwind CSS.
2.	Display the user dashboard after successful login.
3.	Set up department-wise scoping in the backend so users can access data related only to their department.
________________________________________
What I Did
In this task, I focused on creating a functional and responsive interface along with secure authentication.
I began by designing the frontend using React and Tailwind CSS, which helped in building the login, registration, and dashboard pages with a consistent layout.
On the backend, I used FastAPI to create APIs for user registration, login, and data access. I implemented JWT-based authentication to ensure secure login and protected routes.
I also added department-wise scoping, so that users can access content specific to their department after logging in. Finally, I integrated the frontend and backend, tested the data flow, and ensured smooth navigation between pages.
________________________________________
What I Learned
Through this task, I learned the complete workflow of a full-stack web application. My key learnings include:
•	Setting up a React and FastAPI project structure.
•	Using Tailwind CSS to design responsive and modern interfaces.
•	Implementing authentication and authorization using JWT.
•	Handling frontend routing and maintaining protected pages.
•	Connecting frontend and backend through APIs for data exchange.
________________________________________
Outcome
By completing this task, I developed a working version of Brag Board where users can register, log in, and access dashboards based on their department.
The interface is responsive and user-friendly, and it successfully captures and displays user roles and department details securely.
________________________________________
Challenges Faced
While working on this task, I faced a few challenges:
•	CORS issues while connecting the frontend and backend, which I resolved by enabling CORS middleware.
•	JWT validation errors, which required debugging to ensure proper token verification.
•	Styling conflicts in Tailwind CSS during component alignment.
•	Minor routing issues between login and dashboard pages, later fixed through React Router configuration.
________________________________________
Reflection
This task helped me understand how the frontend and backend communicate in a real-world project. I gained confidence in implementing authentication systems, managing state, and designing user-friendly interfaces. It also strengthened my understanding of secure and scalable web application development.
